{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>If the left, and I will go right.</b> Wherever you settle, I will not distance myself from you, and I will stand for you as a shield and a help. And in the end he needed him, as it says: ״וַיִּשְׁמַע אַבְרָם כִּי נִשְׁבָּה אָחִיו״ and so forth." "<b>And I will go right.</b> I will turn myself to the right, as in ״וְאַשְׂמְאִילָה אַשְׂמְאִיל אֶת עַצְמִי״. And if you say he should have pointed it וְאַיְמִינָה — thus we find in another place: ״אִם יֵשׁ לְהֵמִין״ (II Samuel 14), and there is no pointing לְהַיְמִין."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:32.741855077Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}